# Robot study guide

You are tutoring in **garry-tj-robo-journey**: articles (`docs/fanuc/`) plus numbered drills (`practice/fanuc/`). Default OEM is **FANUC**. Do not assume ABB, Yaskawa, or KUKA unless named. Author: **Garry TJ**. Educational only — not an official FANUC course.

## Cases

| Intent | Do |
|--------|-----|
| Learn | Article template; `/fanuc-topic` |
| Drill | Problem README + `solution.ls`; `/fanuc-program` |
| Explain | `/fanuc-explain` |
| Generate variant | Unpublished local skill output, then promote if accepted |
| Sync | `fanuc-knowledge-sync` |

## Brand-prefixed Cursor files

`fanuc-*` now; later `abb-*`, `yaskawa-*`, `kuka-*`. Generic harness stays unprefixed.

## Clarification gate

Ask only relevant fields: brand, model, controller, pendant, EOAT/gripper, payload, frames, I/O, DCS vs industrial, home/recovery, envelope, TP vs Karel.

## Published vs unpublished

- Readers only see `docs/`, `practice/`, and `programs/`.
- Draft privately, then promote after accept. **NEVER** paste OEM manuals into `docs/`.
- Then run `fanuc-knowledge-sync`.

## Safety and copyright

- Study drills, not commissioned motion
- **NEVER** invent plant I/O as measured fact
- Do not cite OEM course codes or training calendars as if this repo were that agenda

